# AI-hint: App-drawer entry for the ShaderGlass overlay: mios-shaderglass toggle attaches a ShaderGlass pane (Wine, RetroArch shaders, Hyprglass glass) to the active window, or removes it. No StartupWMClass: the pane must never be taken for this entry's window.
# AI-related: /usr/bin/mios-shaderglass, src/mios-rs/miosd/src/shaderglass.rs, usr/share/mios/mios.toml [desktop.shaderglass]
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name=ShaderGlass Overlay
GenericName=Shader Overlay
Comment=Shade the active window live with RetroArch shaders (a ShaderGlass pane pinned over it)
Exec=/usr/bin/mios-shaderglass toggle
Icon=video-display
Categories=Utility;Graphics;
Keywords=shader;crt;retro;overlay;shaderglass;filter;scanlines;mios;
Terminal=false
StartupNotify=false
NoDisplay=false
